  "review": {
    "review": "The hero remained alive at full health when the planner exhausted. Decision 2529 (log 7139) blocks descent because the piranha chest remains uncollected; the preceding purchase advanced time without resolving it. The initiating missed preparation appears at decision 2444 (6933): the pool chest and fish are observed while the hero is healthy and not hungry, carrying unknown potions, removable unidentified leather armor and identified uncursed cloth armor. Timed room planning correctly rejects unidentified armor, but unlike flight preparation, pool preparation never considers the carried safe replacement. Source-pinned offline reconstruction matches all 2529 recorded selections and the terminal blocker. On a copy of reconstructed decision-2444 state, the candidate selects the carried cloth armor instead of leaving. A separate equipment-copy probe admits a budgeted pool route and fresh dry test bank without guessing potion identities. No subsequent observations are supplied after the changed decision. The correction preserves fresh potion, protection, hazard and pickup checks. The new regression fails on the original selector and passes on the candidate; the full suite passes 2060 tests with four skips. This establishes preparation, not successful identification or chest retrieval.",
    "learnings": "Before abandoning a required pool chest, check whether carried, identified, uncursed armor can satisfy timed-movement preparation. Seeing a bandolier alone does not establish potion protection. Recheck actual equipment and every potion, entrance, protection and pickup requirement after preparation; never infer unknown colors or waive the chest."
  },
